{
  "title": "Quadriga Effect",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6016/quadriga-effect",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 28 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Quadriga Effect is characterized by an active flexion lag in fingers adjacent to a digit with a previously injured or repaired flexor digitorum profundus tendon.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the inability to fully flex the fingers of the hand adjacent to the injured finger.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation if patient is minimally symptomatic but may involve release of FDP tendon of injured digit if symptoms impact patient's activity demands.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most commonly caused by a **functional shortening** of the FDP tendon due to",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**over-advancement of the FDP** during tendon repair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**>1 cm advancement** associated with quadriga",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**adhesions**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**retraction of the tendon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "\"**over-the-top**\" FDP repair of the distal phalanx after amputation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "FDP tendons of long, ring, and little fingers share a common muscle belly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "therefore excursion of the combined tendons is equal to the shortest tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "improper shortening of a tendon during repair results in inability to fully flex adjacent fingers",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Flexor digitorum profundus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Zones of the flexor tendons",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6016/images/flexor%20zones%203.jpg",
              "caption": "Flexor tendon zones"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most injuries resulting in quadrigia involve Zone I",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inability to fully flex the fingers of the hand adjacent to the injured finger",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "patient may complain of \"weak grip\"",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**upon making a fist the fingers adjacent to the injured digit will not reach full flexion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6016/images/quadrigia%202.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "grip strength decreased",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually not required",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mild symptoms not affecting quality of life",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "release FDP of injured digit",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**severe symptoms limiting function**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
